{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01VWHbEQQGD8i7jXnC12DMB2-call","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:27:29.799Z","payload":{"type":"tool_call","toolCallId":"toolu_bdrk_01VWHbEQQGD8i7jXnC12DMB2","toolName":"subagent_response","args":{"response":"The read side and the \"In the News\" UI are in place. The type-check (`node ./node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit`) passes with exit code 0 and no errors, including whatever is currently in lib/summarize.ts. I didn't touch lib/summarize.ts, lib/types.ts or schema.sql. I haven't run the dev server or loaded a page with real data.\n\n**lib/articles.ts**\n- `getArticles` is unchanged; the import now also brings in `PoliticianNewsSummary`.\n- Added `getNewsSummary(politicianId)`. It queries `politician_news_summaries` by `politician_id` with `.maybeSingle()` and throws on error.\n- It returns null when there's no row. Otherwise it returns the row with `citations` set to `[]` if it isn't an array.\n\n**app/politicians/[slug]/CitedText.tsx (new server component, no \"use client\")**\n- `parseCitedText(text, validNumbers, keyPrefix)` is a pure helper. It turns each `[n]` that's in the citations into `<sup><a href=\"#cite-n\" className=\"cite-ref\" aria-label=\"Source n\">[n]</a></sup>` and leaves other markers as plain text.\n- Keys are built from paragraph index plus marker position, so they're stable.\n- The default export `CitedText` splits the summary on blank lines and renders `<div className=\"news-summary\">` with one `<p>` per paragraph.\n\n**app/politicians/[slug]/page.tsx**\n- Added a local `formatDate` helper that matches the one in app/news/page.tsx.\n- The page fetches the summary with `getNewsSummary(politician.id)` inside try/catch, falling back to null, and builds a set of citation numbers.\n- After Career History there's now a `<section aria-labelledby=\"in-the-news\">` with the h2.section-title \"In the News\".\n- If there's no summary, it shows `<p className=\"empty\">` \"No recent news coverage summarized yet.\"\n- If there is one, it renders:\n  - The `.news-disclaimer` note plus \"Updated <date>.\"\n  - `<CitedText>` with the summary.\n  - An `<h3>Sources</h3>` and `<ol className=\"citations\">`, only when there are citations. Each item is `<li id=\"cite-n\" value={n}>`, an external link with `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and a `span.meta-inline` showing \"source · date\".\n- The h2 has an inline `style={{ marginTop: \"2.5rem\" }}` to space it from the timeline. This is the only inline style; you could move it to a CSS class.\n\n**app/globals.css**\n- Appended rules for `.news-disclaimer`, `.news-summary p`, `.cite-ref` and `.citations` (list items, links, `.meta-inline`), all using the existing variables.\n- Beyond what you asked for, I added an underline on `.cite-ref` hover and a small top margin on `.citations`.","files":[{"path":"c:\\Users\\jarba\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Hackachusetts\\Mapachusetts\\app\\politicians\\[slug]\\page.tsx"},{"path":"c:\\Users\\jarba\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Hackachusetts\\Mapachusetts\\app\\politicians\\[slug]\\CitedText.tsx"},{"path":"c:\\Users\\jarba\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Hackachusetts\\Mapachusetts\\lib\\articles.ts"}]},"status":"completed","kind":"other","executionId":"b04c2126-59c7-4c68-b0b7-e3be3a838803","turnId":"b04c2126-59c7-4c68-b0b7-e3be3a838803","actionType":"subagent_response","title":"Subagent Response","_meta":{"kiro":{"agentMode":"vibe","agentSubtaskId":"b5ab2244-1790-4fbe-9e6e-87f02b541766","toolOrigin":"acp","resources":[{"provider":"github","owner":"Mapachusetts","name":"Mapachusetts"}]}},"subExecutionId":"b5ab2244-1790-4fbe-9e6e-87f02b541766"}}
